The average of 6 numbers is 24. If one of the numbers, 30, is removed, what will be the average of the remaining 5 numbers?

A) 22.2
B) 22.8
C) 23.2
D) 23.5

Answer: B) 22.8

Explanation:

Total of 6 numbers:
 6\times24=144 
Remove 30:
144-30=114 $$
Remaining numbers = 5
 New\ Average=\frac{114}{5} $=22.8
